Bones are written to disk in nearly the same format as the level files used by
an active game and stored within a save file between sessions. So they contain
the same information that is saved to disk while the game is in progres.

You can't exhaust a sink, leave the level, come back, and get anything from the
sink the second time, because its "looted" status (that's the actual word used
in the source) is saved to disk while you're off-level. The same happens in a
bones file.

